  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In first step nitration occurs by mixture of concentrated nitric acid and concentrated sulphuric acid. From this step nitrobenzene (A) is produced.</p><p>In next step chlorination of nitrobenzene occurs, nitro group is meta directing which orients the incoming electrophile at meta position which results in formation of compound (B).</p><p>In last step, reduction occurs and nitro group is converted into amino group and produces compound (C).</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0111_42196a34d134.png\" style=\"width: 943px; height: 124px;\" /></p>"
  }
